{"document_id": "DocRED - 4296c4da1f02a3d6", "title": "Knute Nelson", "text": "Knute Nelson ( born Knud Evanger ; February 2 , 1843 April 28 , 1923 ) was an American attorney and politician active in both Wisconsin and Minnesota . A Republican , he served in state and national positions : he was elected to the Wisconsin and Minnesota legislatures , was elected to the U.S. House of Representatives and the United States Senate from Minnesota , and he served as the 12th Governor of Minnesota . He is known for promoting the Nelson Act of 1889 to consolidate the Ojibwe / Chippewa in Minnesota on a western reservation in the state , and require the breakup of their communal land by allotting it to individual households , with sales of the remainder to anyone , including non - natives . This was similar to the Dawes Act of 1887 , which had applied to Native American lands in the Indian Territory .", "entities": {"Event_adf0ebeaa511": {"type": "PER", "mentions": [{"id": "0_m0", "trigger_word": "Knute Nelson", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [0, 2]}]}, "Event_6b2c093d76db": {"type": "PER", "mentions": [{"id": "1_m0", "trigger_word": "Knud Evanger", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [4, 6]}]}, "Event_a457b9ea1ece": {"type": "TIME", "mentions": [{"id": "2_m0", "trigger_word": "February 2 , 1843", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [7, 11]}]}, "Event_021c28ff207a": {"type": "TIME", "mentions": [{"id": "3_m0", "trigger_word": "April 28 , 1923", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [11, 15]}]}, "Event_795addfab43d": {"type": "LOC", "mentions": [{"id": "4_m0", "trigger_word": "American", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [18, 19]}]}, "Event_936c812427a6": {"type": "LOC", "mentions": [{"id": "5_m0", "trigger_word": "Wisconsin", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [25, 26]}, {"id": "5_m1", "trigger_word": "Wisconsin", "sent_id": 1, "offset": [16, 17]}]}, "Event_3052ff3f0d75": {"type": "LOC", "mentions": [{"id": "6_m0", "trigger_word": "Minnesota", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [27, 28]}, {"id": "6_m1", "trigger_word": "Minnesota", "sent_id": 1, "offse