{"document_id": "DocRED - 72971f0f36693b3a", "title": "Washington Place (West Virginia)", "text": "Washington Place ( William Washington House ) is one of the first homes built by freed slaves after the Emancipation Proclamation of 1863 in Hampshire County , West Virginia , United States . Washington Place was built by William and Annie Washington in north Romney between 1863 and 1874 on land given to Annie by her former owner , Susan Blue Parsons of Wappocomo plantation . William Washington later acquired other properties on the hills north of Romney along West Virginia Route 28 and became the first African - American land developer in the state of West Virginia . One of his subdivisions is the \" Blacks Hill \" neighborhood of Romney , adjacent to the Washington Place homestead . Washington Place was bought and restored by Ralph W. Haines , a local attorney and historic preservationist .", "entities": {"Event_b63dfe24eb58": {"type": "LOC", "mentions": [{"id": "0_m0", "trigger_word": "Washington Place", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [0, 2]}, {"id": "0_m1", "trigger_word": "William Washington House", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [3, 6]}, {"id": "0_m2", "trigger_word": "Washington Place", "sent_id": 1, "offset": [0, 2]}, {"id": "0_m3", "trigger_word": "Washington Place", "sent_id": 3, "offset": [17, 19]}, {"id": "0_m4", "trigger_word": "Washington Place", "sent_id": 4, "offset": [0, 2]}]}, "Event_62d9fcc86a80": {"type": "MISC", "mentions": [{"id": "1_m0", "trigger_word": "Emancipation Proclamation", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [19, 21]}]}, "Event_e638eb41734d": {"type": "TIME", "mentions": [{"id": "2_m0", "trigger_word": "1863", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [22, 23]}, {"id": "2_m1", "trigger_word": "1863", "sent_id": 1, "offset": [13, 14]}]}, "Event_7f41659ec54e": {"type": "LOC", "mentions": [{"id": "3_m0", "trigger_word": "Hampshire County", "sent_id": 0, "offset": [24, 26]}]}, "Event_fbe28113ffa0": {"type": "LOC", "mentions": [{"id": "4_m0", "trigger_word": "West Virginia", "sent_id":